      "title": "Addressing Security Alerts: Expired Certificates and Suspicious Login Activity",
      "content_summary": "Covers common security alerts including certificate expiration warnings, suspicious logins, and brute-force attempts, detailing causes and resolution steps.",
      "content_body": "When encountering certificate expiration warnings or suspicious login activity, first verify the status of LDAP Connector and Session Controller certificates. Expired certificates often result in access denied errors or audit log gaps. If elevated privileges or account lockouts are observed, check for improper access reviews or unpropagated credential rotations. Resolve these issues by renewing certificates, completing access reviews, and propagating credential rotations across all systems."
